{
  "_doc": "How the world is planted. A rule is a species: how thick it grows, where it will stand, and what it grows along. `density` is instances per hectare before the region multiplier; `region_density` overrides that multiplier for one landform, because a wood is not a downland copse at a slightly higher density. `cluster` gates the species through a low-frequency field so it comes in copses and belts with open ground between, rather than an even sprinkle. `near_water`, `near_hedge` and `near_lane` are attraction bands [from_m, to_m, strength]: willows follow the watercourses, thorn follows the field boundaries, limes follow the lanes. Exclusion alone can only ever produce confetti.",
